#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Compiler benchmark: generates synthetic programs and measures check/compile/build/run.

HOW TO ADD A LANGUAGE
---------------------
Insert ONE contiguous block into the section "LANGUAGE BLOCKS" below (anywhere; blocks are
processed in registration order). A block consists of:

    1. the `bm_<Lang>` runner function(s) that invoke the compiler(s), and
    2. one `register_language(LangSupport(...))` call that describes everything else:
       compiler names, file extension, 64-bit int type, supported ops / templated variants,
       version probing, tier, aliases, argument limits, and every piece of source-code
       generation (prefix, function emitter, main header/vars/calls/postfix, quirks such as
       a custom program directory, source file name, section ordering, or compiler command).

Nothing outside the block needs to change. The generic engine (below the language blocks)
only talks to languages through `LangSupport`.
"""

